From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Emmanuel Varagnat <emmanuel.varagnat@vates.tech>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 22:30:42 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] tapdisk: count the sectors of the requests retried at their
 first issue

tapdisk_vbd_issue_new_requests() counted the sectors of a request only when
its first issue succeeded or completed it. A request failing with an error
that makes it retried, like -EBUSY from the VHD driver while it allocates a
block, was retried from the failed requests without being counted: the
sector counters of tap-ctl stats missed these requests, which happened more
often with the larger indirect requests (test_vm_io saw 256 KiB missing out
of 10 MiB written).

Count the request once it leaves the new requests, whatever the result of
its first issue.

Signed-off-by: Emmanuel Varagnat <emmanuel.varagnat@vates.tech>
---
 drivers/tapdisk-vbd.c | 12 ++++++++----
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/tapdisk-vbd.c b/drivers/tapdisk-vbd.c
index d3252454..b5883cb0 100644
--- a/drivers/tapdisk-vbd.c
+++ b/drivers/tapdisk-vbd.c
@@ -2082,6 +2082,14 @@ tapdisk_vbd_issue_new_requests(td_vbd_queue_t* queue)
 		err = tapdisk_vbd_issue_request(queue, vreq);
 		pthread_mutex_lock(&queue->mutex);
 
+		/*
+		 * Count the request once it left the new requests, also when it
+		 * failed and will be retried from the failed requests (e.g. on
+		 * -EBUSY), which doesn't count it again. vreq must NOT be
+		 * accessed after issuing the request.
+		 */
+		td_sector_count_add(&queue->secs, secs, write);
+
 		/*
 		 * if this request failed, but was not completed,
 		 * we'll back off for a while.
@@ -2090,10 +2098,6 @@ tapdisk_vbd_issue_new_requests(td_vbd_queue_t* queue)
 			pthread_mutex_unlock(&queue->mutex);
 			return err;
 		}
-
-		/* XXX: split counting and add; vreq must NOT be accessed after issuing the
-		        request. */
-		td_sector_count_add(&queue->secs, secs, write);
 	}
 	pthread_mutex_unlock(&queue->mutex);
 
